    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=638021637": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor, Nursing - Milwaukee, WI",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor, Nursing - Milwaukee, WI. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Faculty. Institutional Overview : Alverno College is a private liberal arts college with an internationally acclaimed ability-based program and diverse student body. A Catholic College founded by the School Sisters of Saint Francis, we are dedicated to the undergraduate education of women while serving men and women in our adult and graduate programs. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We provide students with real-life, hands-on experiences in the classroom, in study abroad opportunities and in professional internships related to their major. Application Process: Please ensure your resume and cover letter are uploaded to the application. Candidates selected for employment will be required to submit official transcripts verifying the degree(s) required for the position before employment begins. About Alverno College Alverno College is nationally recognized for its innovative, ability-based curriculum that emphasizes active learning, continuous feedback, and student development. Learn more about our academic programs at https://catalog.alverno.edu/ . Physical Requirements and Work Environment: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. This role requires the ability to communicate effectively, use instructional technology, and work in classroom, laboratory, and/or online learning environments. Laboratory instructors must be able to safely demonstrate and supervise laboratory activities in accordance with established safety procedures. Applicant Accommodations Alverno College is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the recruitment and selection process. Applicants who require an accommodation to complete the application process or participate in an interview should contact the Human Resources Department at hr@alverno.edu . Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace."
