    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=638021632": {
      "title": "Athletic Communications Director",
      "description": "Athletic Communications Director. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Staff. Position Summary The Athletic Communications Director supports the visibility and success of Alverno College Athletics by coordinating athletic communications, managing social media, providing coverage of athletic events, and serving as the primary content creator for the Athletics Department. This position is responsible for updating the athletics website, producing timely news releases, creating promotional content, and collaborating with campus partners to elevate the student-athlete experience. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Alverno College will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please contact HR@alverno.edu. Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to workplace diversity."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=637996547": {
      "title": "Transfer Specialist Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Transfer Specialist Admissions Counselor. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Staff. Position Summary The Transfer Specialist Admissions Counselor serves as the primary point of contact and dedicated specialist for all transfer student recruitment, admissions, and enrollment activities. The Counselor will manage the full transfer student lifecycle, from initial inquiry through enrollment, with particular emphasis on conducting preliminary transcript evaluations and assisting with official credit evaluations, building relationships with community college partners, and implementing strategies to increase transfer student conversion rates. Reporting to the Director of Admissions, the Counselor will serve as the subject-matter expert on transfer credit policies, articulation, and transfer enrollment funnel management. This position is integral to achieving Alverno's enrollment goals and advancing the College's mission of expanding access to higher education for diverse populations, including first-generation students, adult learners, and students from Wisconsin's technical college system. Equal Employment Opportunity Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and applicants. The College prohibits discrimination and harassment based on any characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law."
    },
