    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=587697392": {
      "title": "Site Supervisor - Undergaduate",
      "description": "Site Supervisor - Undergaduate. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Staff .25. Alverno serves a variety of students in our undergraduate education programs including our traditional weekday college program and our paraprofessional to teacher licensure program. In addition, supervisors with initial licensure qualifications might supervise graduate students enrolled in our License to Master of Arts program. We place supervisors in a variety of districts throughout Southeast Wisconsin. The majority of Alverno's placements are in Milwaukee, West Allis, Wauwatosa, and southern districts including Racine and Kenosha. We also have placements in Waukesha, Oconomowoc, Whitefish Bay, South Milwaukee, Sussex, St. Francis, and many more. Our biggest certification areas are regular education K-9th grade, special education K-12th grade. We have a growing population of secondary licensure students as well. We also have many students seeking multiple licenses together and students seeking K-9th grade regular education with bilingual and ESL. Next Steps Alverno has the following module to complete as an initial step for consideration to become an Alverno supervisor: https://tinyurl.com/AlvernoSupervisorTraining Please be thoughtful in your responses. Because Alverno's model is to use narrative feedback loops to support student and faculty growth, this module will help us to see what areas of supervision may best suit you. It will also provide Alverno a record of your licenses and subjects so if it is a good match, we can consider which courses and candidates may be the best suited for matches in the future. Application Process: Please ensure your resume and cover letter are uploaded to the application. Candidates selected for employment will be required to submit official transcripts verifying the degree(s) required for the position before employment begins. About Alverno College Alverno College is nationally recognized for its innovative, ability-based curriculum that emphasizes active learning, continuous feedback, and student development. Learn more about our academic programs at https://catalog.alverno.edu/ . Physical Requirements and Work Environment: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. This role requires the ability to communicate effectively, use instructional technology, and work in classroom, laboratory, and/or online learning environments. Laboratory instructors must be able to safely demonstrate and supervise laboratory activities in accordance with established safety procedures. Applicant Accommodations Alverno College is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the recruitment and selection process. Applicants who require an accommodation to complete the application process or participate in an interview should contact the Human Resources Department at hr@alverno.edu . Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=587695081": {
      "title": "Site Supervisor - Graduate",
      "description": "Site Supervisor - Graduate. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Staff .25. Alverno serves a variety of students in our graduate education programs from traditional post baccalaureates who are serving as emergency teachers to highly experience administrators working toward their doctorate and the Superintendent/District Administrator license. We place supervisors in a variety of districts throughout Southeast Wisconsin. The majority of Alverno's placements are in Milwaukee, West Allis, Wauwatosa, and southern districts including Racine and Kenosha. We also have placements in Waukesha, Oconomowoc, Whitefish Bay, South Milwaukee, Sussex, St. Francis, and many more. Our biggest certification areas are regular education K-9th grade, special education K-12th grade, administrator license, and director of pupil services. We also have many students seeking multiple licenses together and students seeking K-9th grade regular education with bilingual and ESL. Next Steps Alverno has the following module to complete as an initial step for consideration to become an Alverno supervisor: https://tinyurl.com/AlvernoSupervisorTraining. Please be thoughtful in your responses. Because Alverno's model is to use narrative feedback loops to support student and faculty growth, this module will help us to see what areas of supervision may best suit you. It will also provide Alverno a record of your licenses and subjects so if it is a good match, we can consider which courses and candidates may be the best suited for matches in the future. Application Process: Please ensure your resume and cover letter are uploaded to the application. Candidates selected for employment will be required to submit official transcripts verifying the degree(s) required for the position before employment begins. About Alverno College Alverno College is nationally recognized for its innovative, ability-based curriculum that emphasizes active learning, continuous feedback, and student development. Learn more about our academic programs at https://catalog.alverno.edu/ . Physical Requirements and Work Environment: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. This role requires the ability to communicate effectively, use instructional technology, and work in classroom, laboratory, and/or online learning environments. Laboratory instructors must be able to safely demonstrate and supervise laboratory activities in accordance with established safety procedures. Applicant Accommodations Alverno College is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the recruitment and selection process. Applicants who require an accommodation to complete the application process or participate in an interview should contact the Human Resources Department at hr@alverno.edu . Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=587695079": {
      "title": "Nursing Instructor - Mesa, AZ",
      "description": "Nursing Instructor - Mesa, AZ. Job category: Employee type: Adjunct Faculty. Alverno College is a private liberal arts college with an internationally acclaimed ability-based program and diverse student body. A Catholic College founded by the School Sisters of Saint Francis, we are dedicated to the undergraduate education of women while serving men and women in our adult and graduate programs. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We provide students with real-life, hands-on experiences in theclassroom, in study abroad opportunities and in professional internships related to their major. These experiences, among others, have resulted in Alverno College being recognized among the top four Midwest Regional Universities. in the 2018 U.S. News & World Report “Strong Commitment to Teaching” category for the eighth consecutive year. The College is seeking applicants for mulƟple part-Ɵme Instructor posiƟons for the School of Nursing at the Mesa AZ location."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=587695078": {
      "title": "Nursing Instructor",
      "description": "Nursing Instructor. Job category: Employee type: Adjunct Faculty. Alverno College is a private liberal arts college with an internationally acclaimed ability-based program and diverse student body. A Catholic College founded by the School Sisters of Saint Francis, we are dedicated to the undergraduate education of women while serving men and women in our adult and graduate programs. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We provide students with real-life, hands-on experiences in the classroom, in study abroad opportunities and in professional internships related to their major. These experiences, among others, have resulted in Alverno College being recognized among the top four Midwest Regional Universities. in the 2018 U.S. News & World Report “Strong Commitment to Teaching” category for the eighth consecutive year. Application Process: Please ensure your resume and cover letter are uploaded to the application. Candidates selected for employment will be required to submit official transcripts verifying the degree(s) required for the position before employment begins. About Alverno College Alverno College is nationally recognized for its innovative, ability-based curriculum that emphasizes active learning, continuous feedback, and student development. Learn more about our academic programs at https://catalog.alverno.edu/ . Physical Requirements and Work Environment: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. This role requires the ability to communicate effectively, use instructional technology, and work in classroom, laboratory, and/or online learning environments. Laboratory instructors must be able to safely demonstrate and supervise laboratory activities in accordance with established safety procedures. Applicant Accommodations Alverno College is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the recruitment and selection process. Applicants who require an accommodation to complete the application process or participate in an interview should contact the Human Resources Department at hr@alverno.edu . Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=587690390": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Graduate Psychology and Internship Coordinator",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Graduate Psychology and Internship Coordinator. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Faculty. Founded in 1887, Alverno College is a four-year, Catholic liberal arts college for women sponsored by the School Sisters of St. Francis. The college also offers a robust array of graduate and degree completion programs for women and men. Student learning and personal and professional development are the central focus of everyone in the Alverno College community. As Wisconsin’s first designated Hispanic-Serving Institution, Alverno enrolls a highly diverse student body of virtually every demographic and experience. It is an institution that has revered tradition and encouraged innovation for more than 130 years. The Department of Psychology & Social Work seeks applicants for a full-time ten-month faculty position as an Assistant Professor in the Master of Science Community Psychology Program beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. Our department is dedicated to identifying a colleague to support our mission of delivering a graduate program defined by its non-traditional student body and holistic approach to client care in which individuals are seen in the context of their community. Moreover, we are looking for a team member who will join in the program’s commitment to preparing culturally responsive counselors. At Alverno College, full-time employees are eligible for health, dental, vision, disability, and retirement plan enrollment for employees and eligible dependents. Tuition benefits are available for employees and qualified dependents. Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications, education, and experience. Application Process: Please ensure your resume and cover letter are uploaded to the application. Candidates selected for employment will be required to submit official transcripts verifying the degree(s) required for the position before employment begins. About Alverno College Alverno College is nationally recognized for its innovative, ability-based curriculum that emphasizes active learning, continuous feedback, and student development. Learn more about our academic programs at https://catalog.alverno.edu/ . Physical Requirements and Work Environment: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. This role requires the ability to communicate effectively, use instructional technology, and work in classroom, laboratory, and/or online learning environments. Laboratory instructors must be able to safely demonstrate and supervise laboratory activities in accordance with established safety procedures. Applicant Accommodations Alverno College is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the recruitment and selection process. Applicants who require an accommodation to complete the application process or participate in an interview should contact the Human Resources Department at hr@alverno.edu . Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6213991.careers?ShowJob=587690388": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of School Psychology - Bilingual",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of School Psychology - Bilingual. Job category: Employee type: 12-month Faculty. Founded in 1887, Alverno College is a four-year, Catholic liberal arts college for undergraduate women sponsored by the School Sisters of St. Francis. The college also offers a robust array of graduate and degree completion programs for women and men. Student learning and personal and professional development are the central focus of everyone in the Alverno College community. As Wisconsin’s first designated Hispanic-Serving Institution, Alverno enrolls a highly diverse student body of virtually every demographic and experience. It is an institution that has revered tradition and encouraged innovation for more than 130 years. The School Psychology Educational Specialist (Ed.S.) Program invites bilingual English/Spanishapplicants for a full-time, ten-month, Assistant Professor position beginning August 1, 2026. This is an exciting opportunity to be involved in the program’s Multicultural and Multilingual School Psychology specialization program. The position is a full time, faculty exempt position. Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications, education, and experience. Alverno College health, disability, and retirement plan enrollment is available to full-time employees and eligible dependents. Tuition benefits are available for employees and qualified dependents. Application Process: Please ensure your resume and cover letter are uploaded to the application. Candidates selected for employment will be required to submit official transcripts verifying the degree(s) required for the position before employment begins. About Alverno College Alverno College is nationally recognized for its innovative, ability-based curriculum that emphasizes active learning, continuous feedback, and student development. Learn more about our academic programs at https://catalog.alverno.edu/ . Physical Requirements and Work Environment: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. This role requires the ability to communicate effectively, use instructional technology, and work in classroom, laboratory, and/or online learning environments. Laboratory instructors must be able to safely demonstrate and supervise laboratory activities in accordance with established safety procedures. Applicant Accommodations Alverno College is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the recruitment and selection process. Applicants who require an accommodation to complete the application process or participate in an interview should contact the Human Resources Department at hr@alverno.edu . Alverno College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace."
    }
